WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.246
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.546 --> 00:00:08.955
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.255 --> 00:00:15.472
Unit twenty-three: Should / Shouldn't (advice). Today you will give advice about health and study.

4
00:00:15.772 --> 00:00:18.366
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:22.475
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.317 --> 00:00:24.028
Should.

7
00:00:25.017 --> 00:00:26.993
Should means used to give advice.

8
00:00:27.583 --> 00:00:28.735
You should rest.

9
00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:31.352
Your turn. Say: Should.

10
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.085
Should.

11
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:36.689
Shouldn't.

12
00:00:37.683 --> 00:00:40.600
Shouldn't means used to say something is not a good idea.

13
00:00:41.217 --> 00:00:42.671
You shouldn't stay up late.

14
00:00:43.283 --> 00:00:45.994
Your turn. Say: Shouldn't.

15
00:00:48.833 --> 00:00:49.649
Shouldn't.

16
00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:51.489
Advice.

17
00:00:52.483 --> 00:00:55.110
Advice means a suggestion about what to do.

18
00:00:55.717 --> 00:00:57.240
Good advice helps.

19
00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:00.700
Your turn. Say: Advice.

20
00:01:03.533 --> 00:01:04.592
Advice.

21
00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:06.177
Tired.

22
00:01:07.183 --> 00:01:09.508
Tired means needing sleep or rest.

23
00:01:10.117 --> 00:01:11.582
I am tired today.

24
00:01:12.183 --> 00:01:14.766
Your turn. Say: Tired.

25
00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:18.555
Tired.

26
00:01:19.317 --> 00:01:20.051
Sleep.

27
00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:23.665
Sleep means the natural rest of the body at night.

28
00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.692
Sleep is important.

29
00:01:26.283 --> 00:01:28.692
Your turn. Say: Sleep.

30
00:01:31.533 --> 00:01:32.233
Sleep.

31
00:01:32.983 --> 00:01:34.275
Exercise.

32
00:01:35.283 --> 00:01:38.525
Exercise means physical activity that keeps you fit.

33
00:01:39.117 --> 00:01:40.652
Exercise is healthy.

34
00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:43.809
Your turn. Say: Exercise.

35
00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:47.888
Exercise.

36
00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:49.303
Doctor.

37
00:01:50.317 --> 00:01:52.804
Doctor means a person who treats sick people.

38
00:01:53.417 --> 00:01:55.416
See a doctor if you are ill.

39
00:01:56.017 --> 00:01:58.437
Your turn. Say: Doctor.

40
00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:02.324
Doctor.

41
00:02:03.083 --> 00:02:03.957
Healthy.

42
00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:08.018
Healthy means in good condition; good for the body.

43
00:02:08.617 --> 00:02:09.908
Fruit is healthy.

44
00:02:10.517 --> 00:02:12.948
Your turn. Say: Healthy.

45
00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:16.627
Healthy.

46
00:02:17.433 --> 00:02:21.026
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:21.883 --> 00:02:25.348
Visal, I am tired every day. What should I do?

48
00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:34.422
You should sleep earlier and you shouldn't use your phone in bed. Should is for advice. It tells someone what is a good idea.

49
00:02:35.517 --> 00:02:36.727
How do we form it?

50
00:02:37.817 --> 00:02:53.675
Subject + should + base verb: You should drink water. For negatives, shouldn't: You shouldn't skip breakfast. For questions: Should I see a doctor? We do not add s with he or she.

51
00:02:54.783 --> 00:02:56.423
Is there a stronger form?

52
00:02:57.517 --> 00:03:10.913
Yes. Must is stronger, and ought to is similar to should. I think you should… is a soft way to give advice. Always give advice kindly, because it is only a suggestion.

53
00:03:12.067 --> 00:03:13.741
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:14.583 --> 00:03:18.824
Grammar focus: Advice: should and shouldn't plus base verb.

55
00:03:19.124 --> 00:03:20.334
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:22.574
You should sleep earlier.

57
00:03:23.483 --> 00:03:25.471
You shouldn't use your phone in bed.

58
00:03:26.383 --> 00:03:27.756
Should I see a doctor?

59
00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:35.346
Use should + base verb for advice and shouldn't for things that are not a good idea. Should does not change with he, she or it.

60
00:03:36.083 --> 00:03:39.038
Be careful! Don't say: You should to rest.

61
00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.081
Say: You should rest.

62
00:03:43.381 --> 00:03:45.357
Use the base verb after should.

63
00:03:46.167 --> 00:03:48.703
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:50.954
Healthy Advice.

65
00:03:51.254 --> 00:03:53.880
If you are tired, you should sleep earlier.

66
00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:56.727
You shouldn't use your phone in bed.

67
00:03:57.733 --> 00:03:59.942
You should exercise three times a week.

68
00:04:00.933 --> 00:04:03.618
If you feel ill, you should see a doctor.

69
00:04:04.633 --> 00:04:07.782
Healthy food and good sleep are the best advice.

70
00:04:08.867 --> 00:04:12.625
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:13.483 --> 00:04:16.275
You blank drink more water. It is healthy.

72
00:04:16.575 --> 00:04:19.903
A, should. B, shouldn't. C, must to.

73
00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:25.397
The answer is A: should.

74
00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:28.283
You blank eat too much sugar.

75
00:04:28.583 --> 00:04:31.992
A, should. B, shouldn't. C, shall.

76
00:04:35.533 --> 00:04:37.382
The answer is B: shouldn't.

77
00:04:38.517 --> 00:04:40.110
blank I see a doctor?

78
00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:43.773
A, Should. B, Must to. C, Do.

79
00:04:47.333 --> 00:04:48.973
The answer is A: Should.

80
00:04:50.117 --> 00:04:51.791
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:57.358
A, She should goes home.. B, She should go home.. C, She shoulds go home..

82
00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.468
The answer is B: She should go home..

83
00:05:04.617 --> 00:05:08.009
According to the reading, how often should you exercise?

84
00:05:08.309 --> 00:05:12.822
A, three times a week. B, once a year. C, every hour.

85
00:05:16.367 --> 00:05:18.761
The answer is A: three times a week.

86
00:05:19.967 --> 00:05:23.316
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:26.811
Give a friend advice about studying for a test.

88
00:05:35.617 --> 00:05:37.175
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:37.475 --> 00:05:50.300
You should study a little every day and you shouldn't wait until the last night. You should also sleep well before the test. I use should for advice and shouldn't for things that are not a good idea.

90
00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:52.263
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:58.647
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and advice: should and shouldn't plus base verb.

92
00:05:58.947 --> 00:06:03.666
Today's value is wisdom. Think carefully and listen to good advice before you decide.

93
00:06:03.966 --> 00:06:07.036
See you in Unit twenty-four. Goodbye!

94
00:06:07.336 --> 00:06:10.522
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

